From: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thunkgen: sync CompilerInstance VFS before setFileManager (LLVM 22)

LLVM 22 added an assertion in CompilerInstance::setFileManager() that
requires the FileManager's VFS to match the CompilerInstance's VFS.

In runInvocation(), the CompilerInstance is created with a default VFS,
but the FileManager passed in from the clang tooling framework carries
its own VFS. Call setVirtualFileSystem() before setFileManager() to
synchronize them, satisfying the LLVM 22 assertion.

This is the correct fix — the CompilerInstance should use the same VFS
as the FileManager it's given, not its own default.

diff --git a/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp b/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp
+++ b/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp
@@ -813,6 +813,12 @@ bool GenerateThunkLibsActionFactory::runInvocation(std::shared_ptr<clang::Compil
   Compiler.setInvocation(std::move(Invocation));
 #endif
+
+#if LLVM_VERSION_MAJOR >= 22
+  // LLVM 22 asserts that the FileManager's VFS matches the CompilerInstance's
+  // VFS. Sync them before calling setFileManager().
+  Compiler.setVirtualFileSystem(Files->getVirtualFileSystemPtr());
+#endif
   Compiler.setFileManager(Files);
 
   GenerateThunkLibsAction Action(libname, output_filenames, abi);
